+# Authored Markdown knowledge bundle design
+
+## Goal
+
+Convert authored Markdown documents into the existing `KnowledgeBundle` representation so the current bundle writer and import path can consume them. Parsing, identifiers, ordering, pruning, and manifest counts must be deterministic.
+
+## Scope
+
+Included: a new `pharma_agent.domain.corpus.authoring` module with Markdown section splitting, ASCII/Vietnamese slugging, section identifiers, reading-order choices, and bundle construction. Headings, nested heading paths, prose/table blocks, document records, glossary entries, and colloquial mappings use the existing bundle schemas.
+
+Unchanged: bundle schemas, serialization, validation, chunking, embedding, import behavior, authored persistence, and APIs. Existing document keys remain unique within a collection; bundle document keys are collection-qualified.
+
+## Interfaces
+
+- `split_markdown(markdown: str, *, fallback_heading: str) -> list[AuthoredSection]`, where each result exposes `heading: str`, `path: tuple[str, ...]`, `ordinal: int`, and `blocks: list[BlockRecord]`.
+- `slugify(text: str, *, max_length: int = 80) -> str`.
+- `section_key(document_key: str, path: Sequence[str]) -> str`.
+- `section_choices(collection: BundleCollection, documents: Sequence[AuthoredDocument]) -> list[tuple[str, str]]`.
+- `build_bundle(collection: BundleCollection, documents: Sequence[AuthoredDocument], glossary: list[GlossaryEntry], colloquial: list[ColloquialMappingRecord]) -> KnowledgeBundle`.
+
+`AuthoredDocument` is the input record carrying the existing `DocumentRecord` metadata and Markdown content (title, key, kind, source, attributes, markdown). The returned bundle uses existing `DocumentRecord`, `SectionRecord`, and manifest models.
+
+## Approach
+
+Keep this as a pure domain transformation beside `bundle.py`. Parse ATX headings outside fenced code, maintaining a heading stack by level. Content before any heading uses the fallback heading and an empty path. Drop empty sections while assigning contiguous ordinals in output order. Within each section, coalesce consecutive pipe-prefixed lines into a table block and assign document-wide `t1`, `t2`, etc.; non-table runs become stripped prose blocks. Build section identifiers from collection-qualified document keys and path slugs. Sort documents by key while preserving each document's reading order. Filter colloquial section references against generated section keys. Populate manifest collection metadata and counts with stable generator values and empty file metadata; the existing writer computes file digests.
+
+## Testing
+
+Add focused domain tests for nested headings, fenced-code heading text, fallback and empty sections, table/prose runs and numbering, Vietnamese slugging and truncation, keys, reading-order labels, document qualification, sorted bundle content, dangling mapping removal, manifest counts, and deterministic bundle serialization/digest after `write_bundle`.
